<p>This policy explains which personal data Rendetto processes, why, how long we keep it and what rights you have under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>

<h2>Who processes the data</h2>
<p><%= t('company.legalName') %>, a <%= t('company.legalForm') %>, company number (EIK)&nbsp;<%= company.eik %>, ul. Samuil 3, <%= company.postalCode %> Bobov Dol, Kyustendil Province, Bulgaria, phone&nbsp;<a class="nowrap" href="<%= company.phoneHref %>"><%= company.phone %></a>. For questions about personal data, write to <a href="mailto:<%= privacyEmail %>"><%= privacyEmail %></a>.</p>

<h2>Which data, why and for how long</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="stack">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Why</th><th scope="col">Legal basis</th><th scope="col">Kept for</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Data">Email, name, language, password hash (Argon2id)</td><td data-label="Why">Your account and signing in to it</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Contract, Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR</td><td data-label="Kept for">As long as the account exists; a sign-up whose email is never confirmed is deleted after 7 days</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Data">Your projects: furniture type, sizes, materials, project name</td><td data-label="Why">The service itself: model, cut list, drawings, machine files</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Contract</td><td data-label="Kept for">Until you delete them or the account</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Data">IP address, country derived from the IP address, browser and operating system, result of each sign-in attempt — also for attempts with an email that has no account</td><td data-label="Why">Protecting accounts: spotting someone else's sign-in, locking after password guessing, warning about a new sign-in</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Legitimate interest, Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR</td><td data-label="Kept for">Sign-in history: <%= loginRetentionDays %> days. IP address and country at sign-up and at the last sign-in: as long as the account exists</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Data">Device identifier (HWID): a hash of the device cookie, a hash of the device fingerprint and a short description</td><td data-label="Why">Recognising a known device, an email on sign-in from a new one, spotting repeated trials and shared accounts</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Legitimate interest</td><td data-label="Kept for">A device not used for <%= loginRetentionDays %> days is deleted; the device and fingerprint from sign-up for <%= loginRetentionDays %> days after it; the fingerprint of a sign-in attempt with the sign-in history, <%= loginRetentionDays %> days</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Data">Two-factor protection: secret key (encrypted with AES-256-GCM) and recovery codes (we keep only their HMAC)</td><td data-label="Why">A second factor at sign-in, if you turned it on</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Contract</td><td data-label="Kept for">Until you turn the protection off or delete the account</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Data">Plan, end date, orders (option, price, whether you buy as a consumer or a business, early-start request, version of the terms, message, withdrawal from the contract), plan changes and their amounts</td><td data-label="Why">The trial, the contract for the paid plan, payment, activation and the right of withdrawal</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Contract; legal obligation for accounting records, Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR</td><td data-label="Kept for">As long as the account exists; invoices for as long as accounting law requires</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Data">Audit log: who did what and when to an account, order or project, and from which IP address</td><td data-label="Why">Accountability and protection in a dispute</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Legitimate interest</td><td data-label="Kept for">Entries are kept for 5 years and then deleted; the IP addresses in them for <%= loginRetentionDays %> days. For customers the log keeps the account number, not the email. When the team deletes an account, a SHA-256 hash of the email stays — it proves which account was deleted without keeping the address itself</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p>The email, name and password are needed for an account: without them we cannot create one. The IP address, browser and device are recorded at every sign-in, because without them we cannot protect the account from someone else getting in. Ordering a plan also needs the choices in the order — without them we cannot conclude the contract.</p>

<h2>What “HWID” means here</h2>
<p>Browsers do not give websites the hardware ID of your computer. So by “HWID” we mean a device fingerprint: a hash of details the browser shows to every website — platform, number of cores, memory, colour depth, touch screen and graphics card (vendor and model). Besides the hash we keep a short description: system, browser, screen size, cores, memory, graphics card and time zone (for example “Windows, Chrome 128, 1920 × 1080, 8 CPU”). The fingerprint is computed at sign-in and sign-up — also for a sign-in attempt with an email that has no account; if JavaScript is off, signing in works without it.</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>We use only cookies the service cannot work without or cannot be secured without. We have no advertising, analytics or third-party cookies, so we show no consent banner.</p>
