  <table class="stack">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Duration</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>__Host-rd_sid</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">Your session after signing in</td><td data-label="Duration">Until you sign out; at most 30 days (7 days without activity), 24 hours for staff</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>__Host-rd_dev</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">Recognising the device for sign-in security</td><td data-label="Duration"><%= loginRetentionDays %> days from the last time the sign-in or sign-up page was opened</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>rd_pre</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">Protecting the sign-in and sign-up forms against forged requests (CSRF)</td><td data-label="Duration">2 hours</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>rd_lang</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">The language you chose</td><td data-label="Duration">1 year</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>rd_flash</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">A one-time message after an action (for example “Saved”)</td><td data-label="Duration">1 minute</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2>Who else sees the data</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Hetzner Online GmbH, Germany — the server Rendetto runs on, in a data centre in the European Union.</li>
  <li>Sendinblue SAS (Brevo), France — sending the emails listed under “Emails” below.</li>
  <li>Have I Been Pwned — when you choose a new password, we send only the first 5 characters of its SHA-1 hash to check whether the password has leaked in a breach. The password and the full hash never leave the server.</li>
</ul>
<p>The country of an IP address comes from a DB-IP database (<a href="https://db-ip.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IP Geolocation by DB-IP</a>, licence <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>) stored on our server — the IP address is not sent anywhere. We do not sell data or share it for advertising. We do not transfer personal data outside the European Union; if a Brevo sub-processor processes data outside the EU, the transfer is protected by standard contractual clauses (Art. 46 GDPR).</p>

<h2>Emails</h2>
<p>We send only emails about your account and contract: confirming your email and an email change (with a notice to the old address), password reset and password change, sign-in from a new device, wrong sign-in codes, turning two-factor protection on and off, a reminder 3 days before the trial ends, confirmation of an order and of a withdrawal from the contract, plan changes, a notice when someone tries to sign up with your email, an email to set your password when the team creates an account for you, and confirmation that the account was deleted. We do not send marketing emails.</p>

<h2>Automated decisions</h2>
<p>We make no decisions with legal effects by automated means alone. After 5 wrong passwords, signing in is locked for 15 minutes — a security measure that lifts by itself. Only a member of our team can block an account, and the reason is shown when you try to sign in.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>Connections are HTTPS only. Passwords are stored as Argon2id hashes, two-factor secret keys are encrypted, sessions live on the server and end at once when the password changes or the account is blocked. The admin panel opens only with two-factor protection. Server logs contain no emails, IP addresses or passwords.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and portability. Much of it works directly from your account:</p>
<ul>
  <li>“Profile” — correct your name and email;</li>
  <li>“Data” — download all your data as a JSON file (profile, projects, plan and orders, devices, sign-ins, sessions and the audit log entries about you) and delete the account together with your projects;</li>
  <li>“Security” — active sessions and the devices used to sign in.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Right to object.</strong> You may at any time object, on grounds relating to your particular situation, to the processing of your data based on legitimate interest — the sign-in history, the device and the audit log. We then stop, unless we have compelling legitimate grounds that override your interests or the data is needed for legal claims.</p>
<p>For anything else, write to <a href="mailto:<%= privacyEmail %>"><%= privacyEmail %></a> — we answer within one month. You have the right to lodge a complaint with the Bulgarian Commission for Personal Data Protection: 2 Prof. Tsvetan Lazarov Blvd., Sofia 1592, <a href="https://www.cpdp.bg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.cpdp.bg</a>, or with the supervisory authority of the EU country where you live (in Italy, the Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).</p>

<h2>Minors</h2>
<p>Rendetto is a professional tool and is not meant for people under 16.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If we change this policy materially, we will tell you by email before the change takes effect. The date of the last change is at the top of the page.</p>
